      "raw_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n1.  **Calculate the total amount of money Mulan has initially:**\n    Mulan starts with $\\$40$. Her father gives her $\\$100$.\n    $$40 + 100 = 140$$\n    Mulan now has $\\$140$.\n\n2.  **Calculate the cost of the jeans:**\n    She buys two pairs of jeans at $\\$30$ each.\n    $$2 \\times 30 = 60$$\n    The jeans cost $\\$60$.\n\n3.  **Calculate the total cost of her purchases:**\n    She buys the jeans for $\\$60$ and a bag for $\\$20$.\n    $$60 + 20 = 80$$\n    Her total spending is $\\$80$.\n\n4.  **Calculate the remaining money:**\n    Subtract the total cost of purchases from the total amount of money she has.\n    $$140 - 80 = 60$$\n\nMulan has $\\$60$ left.\n\n#### 60<|im_end|>",
